# GitHub Branches Evidence

This file is intended to hold the real terminal output showing the branches
that exist in your repository and their status. This output can only be
produced by running the commands below in your own local clone of the
repository — it cannot be fabricated here.

## COMMANDS TO RUN

```bash
git branch -a
git status
git branch -vv
```

- `git branch -a` — lists all local and remote-tracking branches
- `git status` — shows the current branch and working tree status
- `git branch -vv` — shows each local branch along with the remote branch it
  tracks and its ahead/behind status

## WHAT THE OUTPUT SHOULD DEMONSTRATE

Your pasted output should clearly show:

- **Branch names** — every branch that exists in the repository (e.g. `main`,
  `bug-fix-typo`, any feature branches you created)
- **Current branch** — which branch is currently checked out (shown with a
  `*` in `git branch -a` output, and explicitly named by `git status`)
- **Tracking/status information** — whether the local branch is up to date
  with, ahead of, or behind its remote counterpart (shown by `git status`
  and `git branch -vv`)

